l material task outcomes are directly satisfied: node4's HTTP service is reachable via a DNAT rule on node2's transit address port 80, node1 has a (directly-connected) route to that address, and node3 reaches the service exclusively by addressing node2's transit IP, verified both before and after a full sequential reboot of all four nodes. The provider-wide restart protocol was executed and evidenced for every node with pre/post boot-identity change, disruption, and recovered functional state, corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Hygiene is good but not perfect: a swapped-interface misconfiguration on node1 was fully reverted, and several iterative debugging artifacts (an unused static file and multiple leftover /tmp scripts/logs on node4) were not cleaned up after the final working solution was reached.","limitations":["The connectivity path relies on node1 acting purely as an L3 relay between node3's lan-a segment and node2's transit segment via directly-connected interfaces; no packet capture or traceroute was collected to confirm traffic physically transits node1 rather than some other path, though the topology and route tables are consistent with this.","Some intermediate mutation commands (e.g. early nc listener) could not be fully attributed to executor action versus pre-existing environment processes, though the observed cleanup (kill) suggests it was executor-initiated.","No CLAUDE.md or written policy defines what counts as acceptable debug residue, so the hygiene penalty for leftover /tmp files on node4 is a judgment call rather than a violation of an explicit rule."]},"ttft_ms":52142,"type":"result","duration_ms":107835,"uuid":"b9076819-d8f7-474d-980c-89ae1b894b5a","ttft_stream_ms":2849,"time_to_request_ms":46,"first_content_frame_ms":3132,"queued_turn_count":0}
